# ===========================================================================
# What is and is not committed, and why.
#
# COMMITTED (deliberately):
#   data/raw/_api_cache/   ~4MB of API responses, keyed by request hash. This is
#                          what makes `make all` reproduce the published numbers
#                          with no network access and no drift as USAspending
#                          posts corrections. It is the snapshot the findings
#                          were computed from.
#   data/raw/*.csv         the deflator source series, same reason.
#   data/samples/          curated outputs small enough to ship, so a fresh clone
#                          can verify the findings and run the tests immediately.
#   outputs/               the dashboard and BI exports are the deliverable.
#
# NOT COMMITTED (regenerable in seconds from the above):
#   data/interim/          tidy extracts
#   data/curated/*.parquet analytical tables
#   *.duckdb               the warehouse
# ===========================================================================

# --- regenerable derived data ---
data/interim/
data/curated/*.parquet
data/curated/*.csv
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# --- bulk archive: far too large to track ---
data/raw/archive/
data/interim/transactions/

# --- keep the reproducibility snapshot ---
!data/raw/_api_cache/
!data/raw/_api_cache/**
!data/raw/*.csv
!data/curated/_manifest.json

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.envrc

# --- notebooks ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- node, used only by the PowerPoint generator ---
node_modules/
package-lock.json
